      ],
      "content": "TRING                 HIGH STREET SP 9211                                            (South side) 11/69                                  Wall to Tring Park -                                      to E of No. 8 GV                                     II Boundary wall. Early C18, probably c.1711 for John Gore. Red brick, with some blue bricks. A 2m high wall mostly in header bond, with special rounded brick-on-edge copings. Built when main road diverted here from crossing park to S of house. Earth swept up to garden side conceals wall which itself was built to conceal traffic on the road where it crosses a grand  vista  to  N  of  house  in  vast  landscaped  scheme  shown  in contemporary engraving. (Richards(1974)25). Listing NGR: SP9255611453"
    }
  ],
